## M8 — React Research Dashboard

Version 0.7.0 includes the browser application under `frontend/`. It supports project upload and public repository registration, rule/ML/hybrid job configuration, live persistent-worker progress, finding and metric exploration, probability and uncertainty inspection, local feature-attribution charts, refactoring recommendations, and trusted model-registry controls.

Local frontend:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Complete deployment:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Open `http://localhost:8080`. See `M8_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md` for the complete workflow.


## M9 - Final Platform Release

Version 0.7.0 completes the platform with Argon2id password hashing, signed JWT access tokens, administrator/analyst/viewer roles, account administration, mutation audit events, integrity-checked JSON/CSV/HTML/PDF reports, paper-oriented holdout and LOGO exports, a role-aware React interface, and hardened development and production Compose stacks.

Run the final release locally:

```bash
codesmell db upgrade
codesmell api serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
# In another terminal
codesmell worker run
# In frontend/
npm install && npm run dev
```

For container deployment, configure `.env` and use `docker compose up --build`. For HTTPS production deployment, use `docker-compose.production.yml` with a strong database password, a randomly generated JWT secret of at least 32 characters, an initial administrator account, and the public domain. See `M9_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md`, `docs/SECURITY.md`, `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`, and `docs/RESEARCH_EVALUATION.md`.
